function meta(){return `<div class="bc"><a href="#home">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Catalog setup</span></div><section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">CATALOG &amp; TRACKING SETUP</span><h1>Connect your product catalog.</h1><p>Prepare verified product data for Meta Commerce Manager before creating a public feed.</p></section><div class="policy-layout"><section class="policy-content"><div class="policy-callout"><span class="callout-mark">!</span><div><b>Catalog not ready to publish</b><p>The storefront still contains sample product names, prices, and stock values, and has no production product images. Publishing these as real offers could mislead customers and lead to catalog disapproval.</p></div></div><h2>Start with the product template</h2><p>Fill in confirmed details and public HTTPS URLs for every product variant. Keep the product IDs stable between updates.</p><a class="btn" href="/meta-catalog-template.csv" download>Download Meta catalog CSV template <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><h2>Before connecting a feed</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Replace all demo items with real product names, descriptions, prices, and inventory.</li><li>Add an accessible HTTPS image URL for every catalog item.</li><li>Host the completed CSV at a stable HTTPS address that Meta can fetch.</li><li>Validate the feed in Commerce Manager, then schedule its updates.</li><li>Install the real Meta Pixel ID from your business account. Keep Conversions API secrets on a server.</li></ol><h2>Tracking status</h2><div class="stats"><div><b>Not connected</b>Meta Pixel</div><div><b>Not connected</b>Conversions API</div><div><b>Not published</b>Product feed URL</div></div><p class="note">This screen is a setup guide, not a protected admin panel. Do not enter credentials or secret tokens here.</p><a class="aside-link" href="/SEO-ADS-SETUP.md" download>Google, ads &amp; catalog launch checklist <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></section><aside class="policy-aside"><span class="eyebrow">GOOGLE SEARCH</span><h2>Get ready to be found.</h2><p>Verify your domain in Search Console and submit the sitemap after replacing preview content and removing noindex.</p><a class="aside-link" href="/sitemap.xml">View sitemap <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="aside-divider"></div><span class="eyebrow">ACCOUNT-SPECIFIC SETUP</span><p>Verification records and Ads / Pixel IDs must come from your own Google and Meta accounts.</p><a class="quick-link" href="/SEO-ADS-SETUP.md" download>Read setup instructions <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></aside></div>`}
